skill: Selenium

@ WebDriver Basics | B
What is Selenium WebDriver?
= An API for automating interactions with a web browser
- A database driver
- A tool that writes requirements
- A load-testing server
? WebDriver sends commands to browsers such as Chrome and Firefox to simulate user actions.

@ WebDriver Basics | I
Which Java statement opens a web page in WebDriver?
= driver.get("https://example.com");
- driver.open("https://example.com");
- driver.navigate("https://example.com");
- driver.load("https://example.com");
? driver.get(url) loads the page and waits for it to finish loading.

@ WebDriver Basics | A
What is the difference between driver.close() and driver.quit()?
= close() closes the current window, quit() ends the whole session and closes all windows
- close() ends the session, quit() closes the current tab only
- They are identical
- quit() only clears cookies
? Use quit() at the end of a test to release the browser driver process.

@ Locators | B
Which locator is generally the fastest and most reliable when a unique id exists?
= By.id
- By.xpath with a long absolute path
- By.tagName
- By.linkText
? Ids are meant to be unique, so By.id is quick and stable.

@ Locators | I
Which call finds a single element using a CSS selector?
= driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#login"))
- driver.findElement(By.css("#login"))
- driver.getElement("#login")
- driver.select("#login")
? By.cssSelector accepts any valid CSS selector.

@ Locators | I
Which exception is thrown when findElement cannot find any matching element?
= NoSuchElementException
- ElementNotFoundError
- NullPointerException
- InvalidSelectorException
? findElements, in contrast, returns an empty list when nothing matches.

@ Locators | A
Which XPath finds a button whose visible text is Login?
= //button[text()='Login']
- /button.text = Login
- //button(Login)
- //text('Login')
? Predicates in square brackets filter elements. text() returns the element's text.

@ Waits | I
Which wait applies globally to every findElement call?
= Implicit wait
- Explicit wait
- Thread.sleep
- Fluent logging
? An implicit wait sets a default polling time for locating elements.

@ Waits | I
Which wait pauses until a specific condition is true, up to a timeout?
= Explicit wait (WebDriverWait with ExpectedConditions)
- Implicit wait
- Thread.sleep
- Page load strategy
? Explicit waits poll for a condition, such as an element being clickable, and continue as soon as it is met.

@ Waits | A
Why is it discouraged to mix implicit and explicit waits?
= They can combine in unpredictable ways and cause unexpectedly long waits
- They are not allowed by the Java compiler
- Explicit waits stop working completely
- Implicit waits delete cookies
? The Selenium documentation advises against mixing them because the resulting timeouts are hard to predict.

@ Handling Elements | I
How do you select a dropdown option by its visible text?
= new Select(element).selectByVisibleText("India");
- element.chooseOption("India");
- driver.select("India");
- element.setText("India");
? The Select helper class works with HTML select elements.

@ Handling Elements | I
How do you switch the driver's focus to a JavaScript alert?
= driver.switchTo().alert()
- driver.alert()
- driver.getAlert()
- driver.focus("alert")
? After switching you can accept(), dismiss() or read the alert text.

@ Handling Elements | I
How do you switch to an iframe in WebDriver?
= driver.switchTo().frame(...)
- driver.frame(...)
- driver.enterFrame(...)
- driver.findFrame(...)
? Elements inside an iframe can be located only after switching to it.

@ Frameworks and Best Practices | A
What is the Page Object Model?
= A design pattern where each page is a class that holds its locators and actions
- A tool that records user clicks
- A browser extension
- A report format
? POM separates test logic from page details, so a UI change requires an update in one place.

@ Frameworks and Best Practices | I
Which TestNG annotation marks a method as a test?
= @Test
- @Run
- @Case
- @Execute
? TestNG discovers methods annotated with @Test.

@ Frameworks and Best Practices | A
What is the purpose of the TestNG annotation @BeforeMethod?
= It runs before each test method
- It runs once before the whole suite
- It runs after every test method
- It marks a test as skipped
? @BeforeMethod is commonly used to start the browser or reset the state for every test.
